// Designed, not tested. AVNM has no data-plane log of its own. Use these ideas instead:
// 1. Azure Activity log (control plane): who committed or changed a configuration.
AzureActivity
| where OperationNameValue has "Microsoft.Network/networkManagers"
| project TimeGenerated, Caller, OperationNameValue, ActivityStatusValue, ResourceGroup
| order by TimeGenerated desc

// 2. Azure Policy compliance for the dynamic group policy (resource type: policy states, check the table in your workspace).
// 3. VNet flow logs and traffic analytics (Network Watcher) show whether traffic was allowed or denied at the VNet;
//    check current docs for how security admin rule decisions appear in flow log records.
